# Vercel Web Analytics Configuration

## Summary
Configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project. The @vercel/analytics package was already installed but not properly configured.

## Changes Made

### Modified Files:
- **app/layout.tsx** - Updated Analytics component integration:
  1. Changed import from `@vercel/analytics/react` to `@vercel/analytics/next` (recommended for Next.js App Router)
  2. Fixed invalid HTML structure by moving the `<meta>` tag from outside the `<html>` tag into a proper `<head>` section
  3. The `<Analytics />` component was already in place within the `<body>` tag after {children}

### Updated Lock Files:
- **package-lock.json** - Updated to properly resolve @vercel/analytics dependencies after running npm install

## Implementation Details

The Analytics component is correctly placed:
- Imported from `@vercel/analytics/next` (Next.js-specific implementation)
- Placed inside the `<body>` tag, after the main content
- Will automatically track page views and Web Vitals when deployed to Vercel

## Additional Improvements

Fixed an HTML validation issue where a `<meta>` tag was incorrectly placed outside the `<body>` tag. Moved it into a proper `<head>` section to ensure valid HTML structure.

## Testing

✅ Build completed successfully with `npm run build`
✅ TypeScript compilation passed
✅ No new linting errors introduced (existing warnings in other components remain unchanged)
✅ Static pages generated correctly (7 routes)

## Notes

- The @vercel/analytics package was already listed in package.json but needed proper installation and configuration
- No breaking changes or regressions introduced
- Analytics will start collecting data automatically when the application is deployed to Vercel
- No additional configuration or environment variables are required
